    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nAn encoding partition that raises before `q.put()` exits, but the parent waits indefinitely on `q.get()`. Poll the queue with a timeout, inspect child exit codes, and terminate/join remaining workers when reporting a failure. Check sentence-splitting worker exit codes before encoding as well.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted draft. Human author review and NVIDIA GPU/CI validation are pending.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: none; this is a narrowly scoped reproduced bug fix.\n\n## Validation\n\nActual malformed JSON emitted the child JSONDecodeError while the CLI remained blocked after a 20-second observation. Added real-CLI regressions cover malformed JSON, missing input, and successful two-partition merging. Before the patch the two failure cases hit their bounded timeout; after it the CLI reports a worker exit error and exits nonzero.\n\n- Focused CPU validation: **3 passed** using actual production imports and generated fixtures; no production modules or functions are replaced by stubs.\n- Command: `/opt/cpu-review/bin/python -m pytest --confcutdir=tests/unit_tests/data tests/unit_tests/data/test_preprocessing_worker_failure.py -q`.\n- CPU environment: Linux container, Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.8 CPU, real Triton package for imports. `--confcutdir` excludes the parent suite's unrelated GPU/data fixtures; this is not the canonical NVIDIA development image or full distributed test run.\n- Repository `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` completed successfully: Black, isort, Pylint and Ruff blocking checks passed.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [x] I have run the repository autoformatter\n\nNo GPU kernel is added or modified.\n",
